WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.680
The lead in a show that never saw the light of&nbsp;
day. Starring alongside an Oscar nominee with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:11.840
hardly anybody noticing. A detour as a half-alien.&nbsp;
Michelle Trachtenberg has some iconic characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:16.240
under her belt, but it's been a while since&nbsp;
she's been in anything high-profile. Here's why.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.320
Can you envision Michelle&nbsp;
Trachtenberg starring in Twilight?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:24.720
She in fact very nearly landed a role&nbsp;
in the popular vampire franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.440
though it ultimately didn't pan out.&nbsp;
As she revealed to Us Weekly in 2011,

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.040
"There was definitely interest here and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:34.480
there because there's only so&nbsp;
few pale girls in Hollywood."

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.720
But as it turned out, Trachtenberg had&nbsp;
already signed on to other projects that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:42.560
conflicted with Twilight, so she&nbsp;
couldn't commit. As she bemoaned,

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.800
"I guess schedules never worked out."

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.520
Being a part of Twilight would've undoubtedly&nbsp;
lifted Trachtenberg's career to new heights, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.720
maybe if she'd backed out of another project, she&nbsp;
could've made it happen. Regardless, she tries not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.920
to spend too much time looking back and wondering&nbsp;
how things might've been different. As she put it,

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:03.040
"[Hypothetical answers mean] you're&nbsp;
not living in the moment and you're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.800
looking negatively at what you're doing now."

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.960
In 2000, Trachtenberg joined the cast of the&nbsp;
popular supernatural series Buffy the Vampire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:17.120
Slayer for the show's fifth season. She starred as&nbsp;
Dawn Summers, the title character's little sister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:21.120
who proved to be quite pivotal. When&nbsp;
Dawn discovers her true purpose,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:25.760
she struggles to accept who she is and her&nbsp;
mystical connection to every single dimension&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:31.280
of reality. Trachtenberg was grateful for the&nbsp;
opportunity to be part of such an impactful show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:35.920
but she wasn't exactly enthusiastic about&nbsp;
the idea of working on another TV series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:40.080
once it was over. As she admitted&nbsp;
to Entertainment Weekly in 2004,

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:46.000
"Honestly when I left Buffy, I never thought I'd&nbsp;
go back to TV because I've done it. I'm not a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:51.040
person to repeat myself creativity-wise.&nbsp;
And I found TV to be rather stifling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:55.120
especially Buffy. Three years as one&nbsp;
character — where they're not changing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.120 --> 00:02:00.400
the character and your abilities aren't being&nbsp;
tested or challenged — gets very repetitive."

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:03.280
While Trachtenberg did eventually return to TV,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:07.600
her experience of being held back as a&nbsp;
creative individual in front of the camera&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.360
may have very well discouraged her from&nbsp;
accepting other small screen roles.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.200
"What? That's so lame."

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:19.440
Perhaps one of the reasons that Michelle&nbsp;
Trachtenberg became so hesitant to accept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:24.800
certain roles was because some fans of Buffy the&nbsp;
Vampire Slayer responded so negatively to her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:30.000
character. Critical viewers found Dawn Summers&nbsp;
to be annoying, but to Trachtenberg's credit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.480
that might just mean that she played the role&nbsp;
of the annoying little sister incredibly well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:39.600
Still, comments like that have to hurt. To&nbsp;
this day, Trachtenberg says that people still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:45.280
tell her about how much they disliked Dawn. As&nbsp;
she recounted to Entertainment Weekly in 2017,

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:51.040
"I still get comments like, 'Oh my God! I think&nbsp;
Dawn is so annoying!' I get it. It's fine. [...] I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:56.880
rarely get the, 'Oh, she ruined the show.' I&nbsp;
do get a lot of, 'Oh, she was so whiny!' Hi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:02.160
were you a teenager? Oh, you were docile, sitting&nbsp;
in the corner, doe-eyed and happy to be there?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:06.960
No. There's a reason why teenagers have a&nbsp;
stigma, and that is what Joss [Whedon] wrote."

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.160
It may be true that Dawn was&nbsp;
prone to sulking and complaining,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:14.080
but as Trachtenberg notes, she was&nbsp;
at least a realistic character.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:15.600
"What I respect is the fans."

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:22.400
Trachtenberg had a recurring role as Georgina&nbsp;
Sparks on The CW teen drama Gossip Girl from 2008&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:28.640
to 2012, and in the midst of that, she had her&nbsp;
sights set on starring on her very own TV show.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:34.480
In 2010, Vulture reported that the production team&nbsp;
behind Gossip Girl was working on producing a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:40.400
CW drama for Trachtenberg. She was set to star&nbsp;
as a criminology student with a complicated past&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.320
and an uncanny talent for profiling&nbsp;
suspects. The actor had pitched the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:48.240
idea for the show herself, and she&nbsp;
was also set to serve as a producer.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:53.360
Originally, the show was supposed to begin airing&nbsp;
with hour-long episodes in the fall of 2011.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:58.000
This would've represented a big step forward in&nbsp;
Trachtenberg's career. But like so many other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:03.040
interesting series that never see the light of&nbsp;
day, the pilot was simply never picked up. Losing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:08.240
the opportunity to produce and star in her own TV&nbsp;
show was definitely a setback for Trachtenberg.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:13.200
So why haven't Michelle Trachtenberg's more&nbsp;
recent films gotten the same attention as some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.200
of her earlier projects? Well,&nbsp;
after her time on Gossip Girl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:21.040
her subsequent projects simply haven't&nbsp;
earned very many positive reviews.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:25.680
In 2014, Trachtenberg appeared in&nbsp;
the sci-fi thriller The Scribbler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:30.320
which told the story of a woman who attempts to&nbsp;
eliminate her multiple personalities through a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:36.400
risky experimental process. But this comic book&nbsp;
adaptation fell flat among critics and audiences.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:42.480
That same year, Trachtenberg also starred in the&nbsp;
made-for-TV comedy movie Save the Date as a woman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:47.760
who races to find a husband after having a few&nbsp;
too many drinks and booking a wedding venue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:53.360
With middling reviews, Save the Date wasn't&nbsp;
exactly a boon for Trachtenberg's career either.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:58.160
Then in 2015's The Christmas Gift, she&nbsp;
played a curious reporter who tries to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:03.760
track down a stranger who unknowingly changed&nbsp;
her life after sending an anonymous present.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:08.720
Unfortunately, The Christmas Gift didn't make&nbsp;
much of an impression on critics either, so for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:13.920
a couple of years, it seemed like Trachtenberg was&nbsp;
struggling to find roles that truly suited her.

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:20.160
In 2015, Trachtenberg took on a starring role&nbsp;
on the web series Guidance, which was hosted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:26.240
on Verizon's mobile video streaming platform go90.&nbsp;
She played Anna, a guidance counselor who tries to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:31.280
help one of her students investigate the source&nbsp;
of some scandalous photos. She only appeared in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:36.560
the first season, as each season featured a new&nbsp;
cast of characters dealing with different issues.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:41.760
Ultimately, Guidance was canceled after three&nbsp;
seasons. The short episodes just didn't pack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:46.560
enough punch into a few minutes, and critics&nbsp;
and audiences felt relatively neutral about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:50.960
the whole thing. The streaming platform&nbsp;
it was hosted on ended up folding as well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:55.840
as there just wasn't enough interest in what go90&nbsp;
had to offer. While the premise of the series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.840 --> 00:06:01.200
was interesting, most people simply weren't&nbsp;
checking out go90 for any reason whatsoever.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:01.840
"Stickers?"

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.320
"She was big into scrapbooking."

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:05.600
"Who isn't?"

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:06.400
"I love to scrap."

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:13.360
In 2016, Trachtenberg starred as Dallas Baxter&nbsp;
in the Lifetime movie Sister Cities. Based on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:19.280
2006 play of the same name by Colette Freedman,&nbsp;
the plot follows Dallas and her three sisters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:24.080
who've been estranged for years until their&nbsp;
mother's sudden death brings them back together.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:30.640
"Dallas is, is very type A and very particular.&nbsp;
Um, she's a complete perfectionist."

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:36.080
The sisters then must untangle their past&nbsp;
and investigate the strange circumstances&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:41.600
surrounding their mom's death. The result is a&nbsp;
family mystery and a family drama all in one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:46.160
making for a suspenseful narrative, although&nbsp;
it didn't make much of a cultural footprint.

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:50.800
Sister Cities actually did earn a positive&nbsp;
response from audiences, but it wasn't like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:56.080
critics were talking about it nonstop. Those that&nbsp;
did take note of the film generally enjoyed it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.080 --> 00:07:00.240
and it surely helped that it had an Oscar&nbsp;
nominee in its cast in the form of Jacki&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:05.520
Weaver as the mother. Perhaps it flew under the&nbsp;
radar simply because it was a made-for-TV movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:09.280
but whatever the reason, it didn't&nbsp;
do much for Trachtenberg's career.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.960
Trachtenberg has always been&nbsp;
passionate about acting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:16.080
but that doesn't mean she's not&nbsp;
also interested in other showbiz&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:21.840
roles. And as it turns out, she's actually&nbsp;
written several screenplays. It's only natural&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:26.560
that the actor who made a name for herself&nbsp;
as an aspiring writer in Harriet the Spy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:32.560
would be interested in penning her own stories.&nbsp;
As she revealed to Entertainment Weekly in 2017,

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:36.960
"I'm fully WGA and a writer&nbsp;
and have sold several projects.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:40.080
I feel like [I'm living] a Hollywood&nbsp;
version of Harriet's life."

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:44.640
At the time, she was working on two writing&nbsp;
projects that she was particularly passionate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:50.160
about. One was a period piece based on a true&nbsp;
story taking place over 30 years beginning in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:55.760
the 1950s. The other one told the story of an&nbsp;
accessories editor with aspirations of being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:01.200
a writer. Alas, these screenplays never made&nbsp;
it to the screen. Perhaps Trachtenberg is now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:05.440
writing something else, or maybe she's&nbsp;
pushed these plans to the backburner.

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:12.320
In 2018, Trachtenberg lent her voice to the&nbsp;
Facebook web series Human Kind Of. She played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:18.080
Judy Reilly, an awkward teenager who discovers&nbsp;
the unexpected reason she's always felt so out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:23.440
of place, as it turns out that her estranged&nbsp;
father is actually an extraterrestrial.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:27.120
Judy has no idea how she's going&nbsp;
to navigate life as a half-human,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:31.520
half-alien teenager, and it's not as if&nbsp;
high school wasn't hard enough already.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:36.880
But her optimistic mother and her best friend&nbsp;
have her back, and as the series progresses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:41.920
she learns to embrace both sides of her&nbsp;
personality and everything that makes her unique.

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:46.320
Each episode ran about five minutes,&nbsp;
making for an easy and entertaining watch.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:49.520
The series earned decent&nbsp;
reviews, but unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:54.080
it would be another short-lived project for&nbsp;
Trachtenberg, as it lasted for only a single&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:58.160
season. While Trachtenberg has definitely&nbsp;
shown her willingness to think outside the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:04.080
box by taking on projects like this, it hasn't&nbsp;
necessarily translated to mainstream attention.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:06.640
"You have a clot of explaining to do."

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:08.000
"Mom, don't do that."

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:12.880
Trachtenberg had a memorable recurring role&nbsp;
on the original TV version of Gossip Girl.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:17.280
Georgina Sparks stirred up trouble every&nbsp;
time she came back to New York City and was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:22.320
one of those classic characters who viewers&nbsp;
loved to hate. She was simply captivating,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:26.720
and whenever she turned up, you knew&nbsp;
that everything was about to go haywire.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:32.240
Trachtenberg has yet to appear on the Gossip&nbsp;
Girl reboot that premiered on HBO Max in 2021,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:36.880
but that may soon change. According to Josh&nbsp;
Schwartz, who was one of the showrunners&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:41.360
during Gossip Girl's original run and is&nbsp;
also an executive producer for the reboot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:45.280
the production team told the original cast&nbsp;
members that they were welcome to come back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:50.480
for the reboot. But so far, most of them haven't&nbsp;
taken him up on the offer. That is, except for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:55.920
Kristen Bell as the voice of Gossip Girl, as well&nbsp;
as a few other supporting characters. As Schwartz&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.920 --> 00:10:01.040
explained to reporters during the Television&nbsp;
Critics Association summer press tour in 2019,

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:05.840
"We've reached out to all of them to let them know&nbsp;
it was happening, and we'd love for them to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:10.400
involved if they want to be involved but certainly&nbsp;
didn't want to make it contingent upon [them being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:14.560
involved]. They played these characters&nbsp;
for six years, and if they felt like they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:20.400
were good with that, we want to respect that, but&nbsp;
obviously... it would be great to see them again."

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:25.760
After wrapping up Human Kind Of, it seemed&nbsp;
like Trachtenberg went on a bit of a hiatus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:31.280
for a while. For a few years, she didn't appear on&nbsp;
screen at all, and her upcoming slate doesn't look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:36.800
terribly busy. However, she has spent some time&nbsp;
teasing a new project that she'd been working&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:42.880
on behind the scenes, and early in 2021, she&nbsp;
revealed just what she'd been waiting to unveil:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:48.480
a true crime show. She excitedly shared the news&nbsp;
with her fans on Instagram, as she announced,

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:53.280
"The cat's out of the bag. Excited to share&nbsp;
that soon, you can watch me as the host and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:59.120
executive producer of my new true crime show&nbsp;
Meet, Marry, Murder. Do you really know the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:03.520
person you go to sleep with every night?&nbsp;
Stay tuned.....it's going to be killer."

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:05.840
"Be careful who you sleep with at night."

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:11.280
Trachtenberg has been a fan of true crime for&nbsp;
a while. She even wrote a screenplay about a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:16.960
serial killer years ago. So clearly, this&nbsp;
show must be a major accomplishment for her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:23.120
Meet, Marry, Murder Season 1 aired on Tubi in&nbsp;
2021, so maybe it won't be long before we stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:28.320
thinking of Michelle Trachtenberg as a mere relic&nbsp;
of the early and mid-2000s. Hollywood may have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:33.440
seemingly lost interest in her for a while, but it&nbsp;
sounds like she's not quite done with Hollywood.

